<article class="env-exercise" id="028F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/028F">Exercise <span data-tag="028F">111.30.8</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $\alpha : K^\bullet \to L^\bullet $ be a morphism of bounded below complexes of $\text{Fil}^ f(\mathcal{A})$. (Note the superscript $f$.) Show that the following are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\alpha $ is a filtered quasi-isomorphism, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for each $p \in \mathbf{Z}$ the map $\alpha : F^ pK^\bullet \to F^ pL^\bullet $ is a quasi-isomorphism, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for each $p \in \mathbf{Z}$ the map $\alpha : K^\bullet /F^ pK^\bullet \to L^\bullet /F^ pL^\bullet $ is a quasi-isomorphism, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the cone of $\alpha $ (see Derived Categories, Definition <a href="/tag/014E" data-tag="014E">13.9.1</a>) is a filtered acyclic complex. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Moreover, show that if $\alpha $ is a filtered quasi-isomorphism then $\alpha $ is also a usual quasi-isomorphism. </p>
</article>